stateDiagram-v2
  accTitle: Ready is different from running
  accDescr: Created work becomes ready and is dispatched to running. Running work can be preempted back to ready, block while waiting for I/O or synchronization, or terminate. A waiting operation becomes ready when its wait condition is satisfied; only a scheduler dispatch makes it run.
  direction TB
  [*] --> Created
  Created --> Ready : admitted
  Ready --> Running : dispatch
  Running --> Ready : preempt / yield
  Running --> Waiting : block
  Waiting --> Ready : wait satisfied
  Running --> Terminated : exit
  classDef pending fill:#FFFBEB,stroke:#B45309,color:#111827;
  classDef success fill:#DCFCE7,stroke:#15803D,color:#111827;
  class Ready,Waiting pending
  class Running success


